WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.960
Scarlett Johansson should star in a solo Black
Widow movie.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:10.080
Considering she made her first appearance
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe before Thor,

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.300
Captain America, Ant-Man, and the Guardians
of the Galaxy, it seems like Black Widow is

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.920
long overdue for her own top-billed adventure.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:25.070
Yet despite the fact that fans overwhelmingly
voted in favor of Widow getting her own film

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:31.760
over any other supporting MCU character, and
the fact that Johansson was named the highest-grossing

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:37.350
actress of all time in 2016, Marvel still
hasn’t announced a solo project.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.809
So why won't Marvel give Black Widow a movie?

00:00:40.809 --> 00:00:42.800
Best supporting superhero

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.800
One of the reasons Black Widow is so popular
is that she's served as an excellent foil

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:53.320
to characters like Iron Man and Captain America
since her first MCU appearance.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.559
That's not to diminish her importance as a
character and hero in her own right.

00:00:57.559 --> 00:01:03.149
But if Marvel elevates Black Widow to top-billing
status, it'll be trickier for her to come

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:07.869
back to fill the hugely important supporting
roles she's provided.

00:01:07.869 --> 00:01:10.540
Not every character is built for starring
roles.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:15.110
That's why we still haven't gotten a movie
based on Robin's solo adventures, despite

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:19.659
the fact that he's one of the most recognizable
characters around.

00:01:19.659 --> 00:01:21.530
"Holy Shrinkage"

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:22.570
Grounded

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:27.469
Compared with her Avengers colleagues, Black
Widow stands out as underpowered.

00:01:27.469 --> 00:01:32.820
Marvel movies showcase characters doing amazing,
unbelievable things, often with the help of

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:38.409
super-soldier serum, gamma rays, sci-fi suits,
or magic hammers.

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:42.479
But Black Widow works best as a ground-level
secret agent.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:48.009
A Black Widow spy movie would be absolutely
awesome, and could put any Jason Bourne or

00:01:48.009 --> 00:01:53.939
James Bond adventure to shame…but it wouldn't
really be a Marvel movie any more than a rom-com

00:01:53.939 --> 00:01:54.939
would.

00:01:54.939 --> 00:01:56.439
"Hey, I'm Ultron"

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:58.440
"Black Widow"

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.720
"You wanna grab a coffee?"

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.819
"I don't really have time to date any guys
now"

00:02:03.819 --> 00:02:06.039
"What about robots?"

00:02:06.039 --> 00:02:07.530
"He He"

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.250
Not iconic enough

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:13.010
They say a hero is only as good as his or
her villains.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:19.640
So, with that in mind, take a moment and think
about your favorite Black Widow villain.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:20.640
Who'd you pick?

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.230
That's right: probably no one.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:28.171
Unlike the rogues galleries that pester Cap,
Thor, and even Batman and Superman, there

00:02:28.171 --> 00:02:33.070
really are no awesome, immediately recognizable
baddies for Black Widow to fight.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:38.170
While that weakness hasn't stopped other superheroes
from earning their own movies, it could be

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:41.790
another reason Marvel's waited to give her
one.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.690
Toying with fans

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:49.120
Summer blockbusters are often two-hour toy,
bedsheet, and backpack commercials, designed

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.230
to sell merchandise to as many kids and collectors
as possible.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:59.480
So let's recall the controversy from 2015,
when Disney and Marvel's decided to largely

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:04.360
exclude Black Widow from Avengers: Age of
Ultron toy lines.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:11.160
And in May 2016, news hit that Iron Man 3's
villain was switched from a female to a male

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:17.620
before filming began for one reason: "that
toy won't sell as well if it's a female."

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:24.200
"What you just said is one of the most insanely
idiotic things I have ever heard."

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:29.750
Of course, Disney also faced massive backlash
over this kind of thinking over the company's

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:36.460
decision to under-include Rey in the Star
Wars action figure line, so maybe the company's

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.590
finally learned its lesson.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:44.730
And that might help a Black Widow movie — action
figures and all — finally move forward.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.480
Hope for Black Widow

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:53.040
Since 2007, Marvel Studios President Kevin
Feige answered to eccentric Marvel Entertainment

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:59.760
CEO Isaac "Ike" Perlmutter, who is so reclusive
he reportedly wore a fake mustache at the

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.930
2008 Iron Man premiere like he was Bobby Valentine
or something.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:10.770
Perlmutter was also reportedly behind that
Iron Man 3 villain gender swap decision, among

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:11.800
others.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:18.030
But in August 2015, a little over five years
after Disney acquired Marvel proper, corporate

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:23.930
reshuffling resulted in Marvel Studios being
directly absorbed by Walt Disney Studios,

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:27.360
freeing Feige from Perlmutter’s control.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.360
Party!

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.960
So how does that affect Black Widow fans?

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:36.650
It means that Feige may be able to make good
on his comments from May of 2016, when he

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:42.570
said that he was committed to a solo Black
Widow movie actually happening sometime by

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:43.570
2020.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:48.960
After Walt Disney Studios absorbed Marvel
Studios, he finally had the power to put those

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.500
plans into motion without Perlmutter's interference.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:58.600
Whether or not Johansson will still be available
and interested to take this movie on is anybody's

00:04:58.600 --> 00:04:59.600
guess.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.030
But for now, the possibility is greater than
ever before.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.280
Here's hoping it happens.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:05.280
Thanks for watching!

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.320
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:13.129
And leave us a comment to let us know why
you think Black Widow should get a movie…

